Hi,
I found an Alpha emulator that runs on Windows called FreeAXP[1] which I 
tried booting OpenBSD on, It's capable of booting off an OpenBSD iso but 
as the 53c810AP (KZPAA) is not supported by siop(4), the kernel is 
unable to configure the controller.
Is it just a case of adding the missing device IDs for the controller or 
does siop(4) need further work to support the controller?


Sevan

